'''''Carex pairae''''' is a species of perennial grass in the family [[Cyperaceae]] (sedges). They have a self-supporting growth form and simple, broad leaves. Individuals can grow to 0.21 m tall.<ref>{{Cite web|title=''Carex pairae'' F.W.Schultz - Encyclopedia of Life|url=https://eol.org/pages/1123743|access-date=2022-02-04|website=eol.org}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|last=Mifsud|first=Stephen|date=2002-08-23|title=''Carex pairae'' (Paira's rough sedge) : MaltaWildPlants.com - the online Flora of the Maltese Islands.|url=https://www.maltawildplants.com/CYPR/Carex_pairae.php|access-date=2022-02-08|website=www.maltawildplants.com|language=en-us}}</ref> The species is native to Europe, North Africa and Turkey.<ref name=POWO/>

